======================================================================
3. Algorithms re-implemented from published work
======================================================================
PRISM contains no source code from the projects below. It re-implements
ideas described in their papers and repositories; docs/MINED.md records
what was taken from where.

- Fuzz4All (https://github.com/fuzz4all/fuzz4all) — "Fuzz4All: Universal
  Fuzzing with Large Language Models", Chunqiu Steven Xia, Matteo Paltenghi,
  Jia Le Tian, Michael Pradel and Lingming Zhang, ICSE 2024. Licensed under
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0). PRISM's
  autoprompt / mutate loop in prism/fuse.py and src/prism/ is a
  reimplementation of the Fuzz4All algorithm; this notice is the
  attribution CC-BY-4.0 requires. Changes: rewritten from scratch in
  Python and C++, driven by a local model, and bounded by PRISM's laws
  (model output is HYPOTHESIS until a checker confirms it).
- FuSeBMC (Kaled Alshmrany, Rafael Menezes, Mikhail Gadelha, Lucas
  Cordeiro) — goal labelling + BMC-guided fuzzing, re-implemented from the
  published papers.
- AFL++ — the "interesting values" tables used by PRISM's havoc mutator
  (src/prism/havoc.cpp, src/cuda/mutate.cu) are the well-known constants
  from AFL/AFL++ include/config.h (facts, not expression).
- KLEE, Frama-C WP, CBMC, ESBMC, cppcheck, Coccinelle, Infer, Semgrep,
  Strix, RapidCheck — design ideas only; see docs/MINED.md.

